    {
      "id": "HUD-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-hermitian-density-product",
      "title": "Self-dual densities and the discriminant factor of the one-vector mean",
      "statement": "At a unit the finite density for self-dual measures is (Q^t)^(1/2−M)(1−η^M Q^(−M)). Multiplying by the real factors 2^M|λ|^(M−1/2)d gives m∏d, where m=2^(Mf)|disc F|^(1/2−M)/L_M=(2ν_E)^(f/2)ν_E^(−Mf)/L_M.",
      "hypotheses": "F totally real of degree f, E/F quadratic CM and unramified at every finite place, finite completed lattices self-dual, a single nontrivial adelic additive character trivial on F, and compatible Fourier self-dual measures. M≥2 for the convergent inverse Euler product, M≥3 for the rank comparison. In the compact mean the tests at real places are nonnegative smooth compactly supported functions with densities off zero. The Gaussian follows by the cutoff argument in HRV-01.",
      "definitions": [
        "The annihilator of O_u is π^(−t_u)O_u. λ_v is the real character frequency, ν_E=|disc E|^(1/(2f))/2."
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "HUD-01",
        "OVM-03"
      ],
